00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.200
One way that helped me
understand kinda the

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.570
difference between the
machine learning and

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.480
kinda like what we traditionally
think of programming is

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.743
to kinda compare the two;

00:04:49.087 --> 00:04:53.870
So in programming, when you're
in computer programming you

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.780
have data, so you have like
data coming from a data base or

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.650
something else or input by a user,

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.190
and you have rules so like those are the

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.610
functions you write as a programmer,

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.990
like if than statements and all that.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:10.860
And then you combine those together and

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.233
you get out predictable output.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.980
Because it's written by humans it's

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.340
mostly predictable output,
but ya know there are ways to

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.483
write tests to make it better.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.870
And the rules are written by humans,

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.820
so like when you're
programming a computer like

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:31.220
there's like you can
kinda trace back in and

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:36.133
step through it and understand
exactly what it's doing.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.790
In contrast, machine learning is data,

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:44.010
so whatever data you're
putting into the system,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:48.983
and then statistical models
that output results with

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:57.240
confidence scores and that's
a lot different than the

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.990
programming which is
really deterministic but in

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:04.887
AI and the outputs of AI
you'll get a result that is

00:06:09.481 --> 00:06:11.470
50 percent one and 50 percent another or

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.183
90 percent one and 10 percent of another.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.520
And the models, the statistical
models their built on

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.470
examples and there's a
black box element to it,

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:27.850
so you're not actually
like manipulating the

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:31.960
outputs directly and you really
can step through them and

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.173
easily understand the logic
that is going into it,

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.530
which is kind of a fundamental
difference between them, it's

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:42.997
what opens up a lot of the
opportunities that AI opens up

00:06:42.997 --> 00:06:45.913
but it also creates its
own set of problems.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:51.530
So what is it good at,
it's good at finding and

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:54.670
following patterns and then
making predictions based on

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:55.623
those patterns.

00:06:57.757 --> 00:07:00.680
And those predictions and
those patterns they can be in

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.650
things that are really squishy,

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.030
like what's inside of an image,

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.980
it can also be really or like
what somebodies trying to

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:10.663
say when their using words to communicate.

00:07:12.816 --> 00:07:15.383
And making predictions
so like based on the

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:19.190
huge amount of data that you put in,

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.810
if you put this one piece of
data into it you expect it

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.503
to come out this way.

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:30.680
It gets better over time
as models are refined and

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.810
we're all kinda experiencing this as it

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:38.170
goes particularly with like
big companies like Google as

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:40.220
it's getting better at
reading our email and

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.610
understanding like what we're trying to

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.593
say when we're talking to our
Google Home, things like that.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:49.350
And really the biggest
fundamental difference and

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.220
biggest fundamental opportunity that the

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.370
machine learning and AI
provides is that it's the

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:58.500
first time that computers and
content management systems can

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.173
really see into the complex
stuff that is images or

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.130
like human to human communication.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:13.520
Before, sorry, before that was like

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.390
content management systems just is like

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.130
a place where you'd put stuff but it

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.430
really has no idea what's in there and

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.940
it kinda doesn't care.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.870
And this is the first time where your

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:24.640
content management system can start to

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:26.333
actually read what you write.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.900
So like there are some risks or there are

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.500
things that they're not good at.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.710
The building of models
takes time and iteration,

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:41.360
so because its not
deterministic it takes like

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:43.290
creating models, testing
them out seeing what the

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.623
outputs are like and experimentation.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.310
It can very easily amplify bias and

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.660
I'm sure everybody here
has heard stories about how

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:59.010
facial recognition doesn't
work with people of color and

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:03.043
things like that, and
that's a very real concern.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:08.100
And the other one is that
to really get good it

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:13.100
requires very vast datasets
and constant cultivation.

00:09:16.156 --> 00:09:18.780
And for most small
organizations like those are

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.900
kinda like the stumbling
blocks and where AI and

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.473
machine learning don't
become viable solutions,

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:30.030
but there's lots of ways
to sorta tap into the

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:32.560
work that companies like
Google and Microsoft are

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:35.470
doing in this space to get access to

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:38.510
those really big datasets and
sorta the outputs of them.

