will actually tag your
images that you upload to

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.288
Drupal with all the same tags
that I was talking about in

00:16:31.288 --> 00:16:32.530
Google Photos.

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:36.170
So if you upload a picture of a girl or a

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:38.290
picture that has the color pink in it in

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:40.710
your CMS those will also be tagged so

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:44.240
you can more easily find them
and attach them to content.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:48.380
There's also a set of tools
called intelligent content tools

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:51.710
and they require installing
Python and some flasks and

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.910
stuff like that but once
you get it running it'll

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:55.910
actually do automatic summaries for you,

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.130
which is pretty fascinating
and pretty interesting.

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:01.880
I haven't played around with it directly,

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:06.150
but it does look like it
does what it says on the box.

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.600
And this is just the start
so in a way I think it's

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:13.480
not that like they're
AI isn't being used for

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:16.240
content creation it's that
these tools kinda aren't

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:20.363
filtering down into the
layer that we live in, right?

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:28.230
So, next I want to jump
into a little bit of

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:29.670
like what these API's are like,

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.670
and what can be leveraged
and where we can kinda go

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.773
immediately in the near future.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:44.130
And because this is something
we've been thinking about,

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:47.680
we created a demo called Happygram.AI

00:17:50.574 --> 00:17:53.010
and you can actually try
it out later today and

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:56.420
what it does is it collects
a happy moment from you,

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:59.230
and then illustrates it using images from

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:02.740
Unsplash using some of the
API's that I'm talking about.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:06.720
It's kinda a fun way to see
what is potentially possible,

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:11.720
but also showcases how you
can use these technologies to

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:15.043
make content creation more streamlined.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.640
So I'm gonna be talking about the

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:22.840
tools that Google provides but all the

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:25.050
cloud providers including AWS,

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:28.120
and Microsoft Azure, and Google,

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.540
and IBM Watson all have
these capabilities and

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.480
they're very comparable between them.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.850
There's kinda subtle
differences in the capabilities,

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:39.350
subtle differences in what
they do and pricing but like

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:41.560
it's really interchangeable
depending on yeah

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:46.560
which platform your on
they're probably available.

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:50.150
So the first one is the

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:52.810
Google Natural Language Processing tools,

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:57.080
and what they do is that
they give you a lot of

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:59.890
analysis of text that you put into it.

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:02.680
So they analyze sentiment
so telling you how

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:04.984
positive or negative a piece of content is

00:19:04.984 --> 00:19:08.360
so they're useful for things
like moderation of comments,

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:13.360
also in trying to understand
customer interactions with you.

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:17.080
But also can be a tool
for writers if they're to

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:20.930
be able to kinda provide
them with feedback about the

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:22.300
content that they're writing, right?

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:25.480
If they think that they're
writing something happy but

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:27.840
Google comes back and says
it's not really that happy,

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:30.010
that could be a sign that
there's a different way to

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:30.843
word things.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:34.390
It provides a very
in-depth analysis of the

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:38.650
parts of speech and what
content is about but

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.610
then also how the different
words are linked together and

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:46.610
you have a very detailed
set of tools to be

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:51.890
able kinda pull out phrases and
associations of words in it.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:58.060
There's a very global
content classification that

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:02.720
happens and you can see
like in Google there's like

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.193
links to the Wikipedia
articles and et cetera.

00:20:07.444 --> 00:20:10.970
And also it provides the
most salient topics in

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:13.270
a piece of text and seeing this in

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.940
action is pretty impressive
because it's not like

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.790
we're kinda used to that with key words or

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:21.490
with a search or something like that,

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.120
but this is different so this is

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:25.340
what the content is really about and it's

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:29.160
prioritized based on how
important the nouns or

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.930
the subjects or the
entities as it calls it

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:34.503
are in the parts of speech.

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:43.380
The next API that's probably
the most useful out of

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:46.100
these and the lowest
hanging fruit that's kinda

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:49.140
immediately available and also really easy

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.143
because there's already
a Google integration,

00:20:53.431 --> 00:20:58.431
is an API that classifies
the contents of image it

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:01.540
extracts objects from the images.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.140
And I'll just move to the
slide with puppies anyway.

00:21:06.097 --> 00:21:08.937
And it does a surprisingly
good job at this so

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:14.610
the things that like impress
me when I tried this out is

00:21:14.610 --> 00:21:19.530
not that it finds the dog
but that it tags all three of

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:20.600
the dogs that are in this,

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.790
so two of the dogs you
can't see their faces,

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:26.820
they're looking away and the back one like

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.120
ya know, like it's almost
questionable whether it's

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:30.710
a cat or not, right?

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:32.450
The other thing that it finds is

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:36.210
that these are Labrador
Retrievers, which is

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:39.540
actually questionable in some ways but is

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:41.083
surprisingly accurate.

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:45.410
And then finally, that it
identifies that they're in

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:50.410
a kennel, and to me that's
kinda interesting because

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:54.110
you can't really tell that
the shape of a kennel or

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:55.810
something like that it's just I guess,

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:58.960
dogs with vertical bars in front of it

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:03.720
you know, have a very high probability of

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:04.663
being in a kennel.

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:09.830
So I mean in digging into these things,

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:13.440
and you can try them
out on their website it

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:17.443
is surprisingly powerful
and surprisingly accurate.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:28.180
The last tool is probably
the most powerful and the

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:32.455
one that can provide the
biggest advantages to

00:22:32.455 --> 00:22:34.023
content creators.

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:39.110
And its called Auto ML. And what it is,

00:22:39.110 --> 00:22:42.950
it is a tool that takes
all the complexity out of

00:22:42.950 --> 00:22:46.550
building your own machine
learning models and

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:47.853
gets it out of your way.

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:52.250
It works by you tagging your content,

00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:55.600
a portion of it as the
learning model that it's

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:58.640
going to use, and then uploading
all of your content and

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:00.983
then just running algorithm through it.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:06.143
You can see when you try
the demo out later today,

00:23:07.256 --> 00:23:10.360
we used it to categorize
happy moments and there is

00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:12.630
about seven categorize and it's

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:15.320
right almost every single time.

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:19.480
Which is fascinating
and that can be used to

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:24.650
take content that your
editors are putting in and

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:29.433
tag it with your taxonomy.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:35.927
It can also be used to tag
it with a taxonomy or a

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:38.670
range of taxonomies that would be

00:23:38.670 --> 00:23:43.670
completely pedantic and a
huge burden on your users so

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:46.150
I don't know if anybody here has like a

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:49.100
complicated taxonomy that there's like

00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:51.610
fights around well does it
really belong in this or

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:53.990
does it belong in that and one person is

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:56.590
tagging things one way
but then another person is

00:23:56.590 --> 00:23:59.190
tagging things another way
and it creates a mess and

00:24:00.110 --> 00:24:01.910
makes the content difficult to find.

00:24:03.810 --> 00:24:08.370
Using this tool, that
can all be automated and

00:24:08.370 --> 00:24:12.030
editors can just go back to
just writing and not having to

00:24:12.030 --> 00:24:15.163
worry about all of that types of content.

00:24:16.670 --> 00:24:19.210
The other thing that it
can really help with is

00:24:19.210 --> 00:24:24.210
with SEO, so being able
to take content and

00:24:28.230 --> 00:24:32.020
automatically attach all
the metadata that Google or

00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:35.060
Facebook is looking for
and take that out of

00:24:35.060 --> 00:24:37.083
the writer's way.

00:24:44.130 --> 00:24:49.130
So those are some of the different ways,

00:24:50.612 --> 00:24:53.040
so those are some of the
things that are available.

00:24:53.040 --> 00:24:55.770
But broadly what can it do?

00:24:55.770 --> 00:24:57.930
So it can automate menial tasks,

00:24:57.930 --> 00:25:00.700
so taking things like classification,

00:25:00.700 --> 00:25:05.110
writing metadata,
attaching alt. text out of

00:25:05.110 --> 00:25:08.700
the writers and content
creators day to day.

00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:11.573
Even starting to do things
like summarize text.

00:25:13.590 --> 00:25:18.590
It can also combine data with templates in

00:25:20.450 --> 00:25:24.630
a much smarter way than you can now.

00:25:24.630 --> 00:25:26.890
So right now you can sort of say that like

00:25:26.890 --> 00:25:28.196
okay well this is gonna be content,

00:25:28.196 --> 00:25:29.770
this is gonna be an
image and you kinda like

00:25:29.770 --> 00:25:32.610
you put it into places
and it all fits together.

00:25:32.610 --> 00:25:37.610
But instead now that can
go a layer deeper and

00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:39.970
do something like the BBC where instead of

00:25:39.970 --> 00:25:43.760
talking about you can
localize the content and

00:25:43.760 --> 00:25:45.860
talk about statistics that are relevant to

00:25:45.860 --> 00:25:48.780
the users or write one article,

00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:53.180
use it in different schools
across the campus and

00:25:53.180 --> 00:25:57.503
replace the relevant
information intelligently.

00:26:00.460 --> 00:26:03.810
It can also provide very deep analysis of

00:26:03.810 --> 00:26:08.640
the content and very unbiased
analysis of the content.

00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:11.550
So tools like Hemingway and Grammarly

00:26:11.550 --> 00:26:14.910
can provide feedback to writers
about how their writing is,

00:26:14.910 --> 00:26:17.190
how effective it is, and how its working.

00:26:17.190 --> 00:26:21.890
But it can also provide an entry point to

00:26:22.730 --> 00:26:26.490
all the media that's being
used across campus and

00:26:26.490 --> 00:26:28.900
centralize it and tag
it in ways that make it

00:26:28.900 --> 00:26:32.980
useful to other parts of the campus.

00:26:32.980 --> 00:26:37.402
So like when that, like going back to the

00:26:37.402 --> 00:26:40.573
picture of the puppies inside the kennel,

00:26:43.290 --> 00:26:45.790
probably very likely that if you have a

00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:49.030
very disciplined content creation team if

00:26:49.030 --> 00:26:50.920
they were uploading that
image that they would tag it

00:26:50.920 --> 00:26:54.370
as dogs maybe tag it as puppies but it's

00:26:54.370 --> 00:26:56.620
unlikely that, and where
they took it and things like

00:26:56.620 --> 00:26:59.490
that probably, but it's unlikely
that they would actually

00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:03.710
tag that image with the fact
that they're in a kennel.

00:27:03.710 --> 00:27:05.510
That's kinda like a weird detail,

00:27:05.510 --> 00:27:09.663
that Google picks up
on but if it wasn't an

00:27:12.020 --> 00:27:14.648
article about kennels that
would probably never come up in

00:27:14.648 --> 00:27:18.543
the mind of the content creator, right?

00:27:19.490 --> 00:27:22.860
But here, its just very
pedantically and very

00:27:26.100 --> 00:27:27.720
deeply sort of looking at what's there and

00:27:27.720 --> 00:27:29.670
comparing it to things
that he'd seen before and

00:27:29.670 --> 00:27:32.853
telling you what it thinks is there.

00:27:34.850 --> 00:27:37.810
Another way that this
can be leveraged is to

00:27:37.810 --> 00:27:42.040
provide suggestions to
improve content and take the

00:27:43.450 --> 00:27:46.860
analytics data that is coming in and

00:27:46.860 --> 00:27:49.330
provide suggestions as to
what kinds of headlines or

00:27:49.330 --> 00:27:52.460
how headlines can be re-worded so

00:27:52.460 --> 00:27:55.223
that they're more effective
when the content goes out.

00:27:59.183 --> 00:28:02.430
And then finally a deep
categorization and a

00:28:03.521 --> 00:28:05.963
very unbiased categorization of content.

00:28:10.025 --> 00:28:13.820
So these are all the things
that like are possible or

00:28:13.820 --> 00:28:16.823
can be done with machine learning and AI.

00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:19.583
But there's one very big caveat,

00:28:23.084 --> 00:28:27.313
that when creating models
or putting information into

00:28:27.313 --> 00:28:32.313
a machine learning model it is

00:28:33.280 --> 00:28:36.480
imperative that you really
look very deeply into

00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:39.150
what you're putting into it because it's a

00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:44.150
black box it doesn't lend
itself to easy scrutiny.

00:28:48.960 --> 00:28:53.960
It's very easy to create not
just one piece of content or

00:28:54.270 --> 00:28:59.270
one image that's biased
or that doesn't speak to

00:29:00.720 --> 00:29:04.580
everyone but really kinda create
that problem across campus

00:29:04.580 --> 00:29:08.670
and with when you're doing
things like making suggestions to

00:29:08.670 --> 00:29:11.930
improve content or suggesting images that

00:29:11.930 --> 00:29:15.620
can really reinforce the
bias' that are made by the

00:29:15.620 --> 00:29:19.950
people who are creating
those models, right?

00:29:19.950 --> 00:29:21.890
And it'll happen in subtle ways and

00:29:21.890 --> 00:29:26.890
it'll also happen on a
much grander scale than

00:29:27.070 --> 00:29:28.870
just one person writing one article.

00:29:30.420 --> 00:29:35.420
And that's why ethics and AI
really kinda go together as a

00:29:36.580 --> 00:29:41.200
conversation, it comes up in
the news this way but it's

00:29:41.200 --> 00:29:45.010
not a FUD and its not an exaggeration,

00:29:45.010 --> 00:29:48.640
like this is literally is a tool to

00:29:48.640 --> 00:29:50.413
automate and disseminate bias.

00:29:51.840 --> 00:29:55.320
Google and all the other
and Amazon both have

00:29:56.190 --> 00:30:00.880
extensive portions about their ethics and

00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:03.510
how they're approaching
it and it's gonna work if

00:30:03.510 --> 00:30:05.427
you're kinda diving into this stuff to

00:30:05.427 --> 00:30:08.800
really look at how they're
approaching this and the

00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:10.550
mistakes that they've already made.

00:30:14.630 --> 00:30:15.463
That's it!

00:30:17.299 --> 00:30:19.549
(applause)

